id: pmc-6eau
title: "A test asserts an error that only occurs when no package.json exists anywhere above the OS temp directory, so it fails on a host where one does"
description: "test/release-context.test.ts, 'throws when release-version-from-package finds no package.json', creates a fixture under tmpdir() and asserts resolveReleaseContext walks to the filesystem root without finding a package.json. Its own comment states the assumption out loud: '/tmp itself has none.'\n\nThat is an assumption about the HOST, not about the code. On this development machine /tmp/package.json existed - 60 bytes, created 2026-09-06 by an npx/bunx execution probe, exactly the kind of thing that leaves one behind - so the walk found it and the assertion failed with a message that reads like a production regression:\n\n  The input did not match /requires a package.json in the current directory or an ancestor/.\n  Input: 'Error: /tmp/package.json does not contain a valid version field'\n\nConfirmed pre-existing and environmental: the failure reproduces on origin/main with all local changes stashed, and disappears once the stray file is moved aside. CI has never seen it because a fresh runner has a clean /tmp.\n\nTwo separable problems. The verdict depends on state nobody declared or controls, so it can flip with no commit - the same class as a gate that measures the clock. And when it flips, the failure names the production regex rather than the unmet precondition, so the reader's first hypothesis is a code change that did not happen; this session spent time confirming it was not one.\n\nNeither weakening the assertion nor skipping on an unsuitable host is acceptable, because a skipped test reports as a pass. The test should assert its precondition explicitly so an unsuitable host reports ITSELF, or the search should take a boundary so the case is reachable without depending on the entire filesystem above the fixture."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[2]: flake,testing
created_at: "2026-09-07T11:08:42.695Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-16T04:08:59.493Z"
author: claude
acceptance_criteria: "The test's verdict does not depend on the contents of directories above the fixture; On a host where the precondition does not hold, the failure names the precondition, not the production regex"
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T04:04:42.634Z",codex-agent,"Current-main audit at aafea5d (package 2026.10.15): Already fixed. `a102d18` (#215), included in `v2026.10.4`. `src/release-context.ts:495` implements an inclusive ancestor boundary; `test/release-context.test.ts:158` owns its tree and plants a decoy package above the boundary. The adjacent tests cover inclusive and invalid boundaries. No item is closed; verification and closure remain with the orchestrator."
  "2026-10-16T04:05:10.137Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: changing only findPackageJson to stop at filesystem root instead of packageSearchBoundary makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"throws when release-version-from-package finds no package.json\" test/release-context.test.ts fail 0/1 (Missing expected exception), because it finds the fixture-owned decoy above the boundary. No ambient metadata was changed. Restored focused suite passes."
  "2026-10-16T04:08:55.638Z",codex-agent,"Pinned-host linked verification: pm test pmc-6eau --run --match \"node --test\" --progress passed. Command: node --test test/release-context.test.ts; 38/38 tests, zero failures/cancelled/skipped/todo. Focused combined verification passed 63/63; suffix and invalid-date controls passed 2/2. Test-result tracking is disabled in project settings, so this comment preserves the run receipt without changing that policy."
